# CODEOWNERS — who GitHub requests review from, per path.
#
# Last match wins, so the catch-all comes first and the sensitive surfaces
# below override it. Today there is one maintainer; the point of listing the
# areas separately anyway is that adding a second reviewer is then a one-line
# edit against the area they actually own, not a re-derivation of this file.
#
# An entry here only requests review. Make it *binding* in
# Settings → Branches → main → "Require review from Code Owners"; without that
# branch-protection rule this file is a routing hint, nothing more.

# --- default ------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @rob-c

# --- security-critical: auth, authz, credentials, delegation ------------------
# Every file here decides whether a request speaks for someone. Changes need a
# security negative test (see SECURITY.md), not just a passing suite.
/src/auth/                          @rob-c
/src/fs/vfs/vfs_deleg.c             @rob-c
/client/apps/auth/                  @rob-c
/shared/                            @rob-c
/SECURITY.md                        @rob-c
/docs/07-security/                  @rob-c

# --- the VFS seam (INVARIANT 12) and the storage backends ---------------------
# Raw data syscalls live only below this line; a bypass here is a data-integrity
# or cross-identity bug by construction.
/src/fs/                            @rob-c

# --- wire protocol: anything parsing attacker-controlled bytes ----------------
/src/protocols/                     @rob-c
/src/net/                           @rob-c

# --- build + CI wiring --------------------------------------------------------
# `config` and `client/Makefile` decide what actually gets compiled; the guard
# fleet decides what is enforced. Both have silently stopped working before.
/config                             @rob-c
/client/Makefile                    @rob-c
/CMakeLists.txt                     @rob-c
/tools/ci/                          @rob-c
/tools/git-hooks/                   @rob-c
/.github/                           @rob-c

# --- dependency surface -------------------------------------------------------
# Widening a bound is a supply-chain decision. Review it as one.
/requirements.txt                   @rob-c
/requirements-optional.txt          @rob-c
/requirements-dev.txt               @rob-c
/k8s-tests/pytests/requirements.txt @rob-c

# --- packaging ----------------------------------------------------------------
/packaging/                         @rob-c
